Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• `start_position`: genomic left coordinate of a variant – needed to locate variants inside the BRCA1 span.  
• `end_position`: genomic right coordinate of a variant – needed (together with start_position) to delimit the whole BRCA1 span.  
• `vep` (ARRAY<STRUCT<…>>): holds one VEP record per alternate allele.  
  – `vep.SYMBOL`: gene symbol to find the BRCA1 annotations.  
  – `vep.Consequence`: functional consequence(s); will be searched for the text “missense_variant”.  
  – `vep.Protein_position`: protein residue position (e.g. “125/1863”).  
Conditions that will be used  
• `EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM UNNEST(vep) v WHERE v.SYMBOL='BRCA1')` – variant is annotated to BRCA1.  
• `v.Consequence LIKE '%missense_variant%'` – keep only missense consequences.  
• Coordinates between the previously found MIN(start_position) and MAX(end_position).  

Below are ten progressively‑complex BigQuery queries (all limited to 20 rows for exploration) finishing with the final answer query.  
Replace nothing – identifiers are already fully‑qualified.

```sql
-- 1. Description: peek at raw rows in the chromosome‑17 table
